2026-09-27T07:22:14.7049555Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7050036Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7050473Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7051663Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7052960Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7053084Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7053361Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7053759Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7054163Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7054285Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7054569Z ================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7054764Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7054996Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7055515Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7055867Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7056025Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7056405Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7056647Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7056835Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7057548Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7058047Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7058996Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7060091Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7060260Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7060884Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7061757Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7062214Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7062697Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7063354Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7063480Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7063773Z ========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7063951Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7066073Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7068333Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7068676Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7069655Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7070857Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7071841Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7072761Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7073462Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7155371Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7155946Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7156330Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7156558Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7158189Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7160157Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7161108Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7162383Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:22:14.7162696Z 
